cosmo: slim the default config to what the lua fetch/hash client uses (#186)

The lua binary is a TLS *client* (tool/net/lfetch.c) plus a digest
provider (tool/net/lfuncs.c: MD5/SHA1/SHA2 via the md layer). This
patch disables, in include/mbedtls/mbedtls_config.h only:

- server-side TLS and DTLS (SSL_SRV_C, PROTO_DTLS + its dependent
  options, SSL_COOKIE_C, SSL_CACHE_C, SSL_TICKET_C)      [-86 KB]
- legacy/unused crypto: CAMELLIA, ARIA, DES, RIPEMD160,
  NIST_KW, CMAC, ECJPAKE                                 [-49 KB]
- the SSL debug string machinery and self tests
  (DEBUG_C, SELF_TEST) - no consumer installs a debug
  callback (ERROR_C / mbedtls_strerror stays)            [-74 KB]
- PSA persistent key storage (PSA_CRYPTO_STORAGE_C,
  PSA_ITS_FILE_C) - psa_crypto_init for TLS 1.3 works
  without it                                             [-4 KB]
- X.509/PK/PEM writing, CSR/CRL parsing, PKCS7, and the
  PSK key exchanges a fetch client can never configure   [-4 KB]

Kept deliberately: TLS 1.3 (#185 will unpin it), ECDHE/RSA/DHE key
exchanges and the AES+GCM/CCM/chacha suites browsers and real servers
need, PEM/X.509 parsing, ERROR_C.

Measured on x86_64 default mode: o//tool/lua/lua 3,433,476 ->
3,216,388 bytes (-217 KB, -6.3%). Gates: o//tool/lua/test,
o//test/net/https3, and a live https fetch all pass.
